    "uniprot_function": "Functions as a coreceptor for Wnt/beta-catenin signaling. Essential for axis formation during embryogenesis and bone formation. Together with LRP5, regulates bone mass in a pathway that includes SOST and DKK1. In Wnt-Fzd-LRP5/LRP6 complex, promotes beta-catenin signaling through inducing aggregation of receptor-ligand complexes into ribosome-sized signalosomes. Recruits DVL1 polymers to the plasma membrane which, in turn, recruit the AXIN1/GSK3B-complex to the cell surface promoting the formation of signalosomes and inhibiting AXIN1/GSK3B-mediated phosphorylation and destruction of beta-catenin. Undergoes gamma-secretase-dependent regulated intramembrane proteolysis releasing an intracellular domain that can bind GSK3B and activate canonical Wnt signaling. Acts as a receptor for R-spondins (RSPO1, RSPO2, RSPO3), potentiating Wnt signaling. Wnt signaling is further regulated by ubiquitination via ZNRF3/RNF43.",
    "catalytic_activity": null,
