    "pathway_role_summary": "LRP6 is an essential co-receptor for canonical Wnt/beta-catenin signaling. Upon Wnt binding with Frizzled receptors, LRP6 undergoes phosphorylation at cytoplasmic PPPSP motifs, recruits DVL and the AXIN/GSK3B destruction complex to the membrane, leading to beta-catenin stabilization and nuclear translocation. LRP6 activity is negatively regulated by DKK1/Kremen-mediated endocytosis, SOST binding, and ZNRF3/RNF43-mediated ubiquitination, while R-spondins potentiate signaling by blocking ubiquitin ligases. LRP6 plays critical roles in embryonic axis formation, bone formation, and tissue homeostasis."
  },
