    "data_quality_notes": "Comprehensive coverage of LRP6 structure, function, and interactions. Kinetic data available for key interactions (DKK1, SOST, Wnt3a, GSK3B). Multiple crystal structures and cryo-EM data available. Extensive PTM data including phosphorylation, ubiquitination, palmitoylation, and N-glycosylation sites. Some quantitative kinetic parameters (Km, Kcat, kon, koff) available from literature but not all interactions have been fully characterized kinetically. C-terminal disordered region (1556-1613) likely has low AlphaFold confidence.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "LRP6 is a critical hub protein in canonical Wnt signaling with multiple regulatory layers: (1) Extracellular regulation by Wnt ligands, DKK1/SOST antagonists, and R-spondins; (2) Membrane-proximal regulation by phosphorylation (GRK5/6, CDK14, GSK3B, CK1), palmitoylation, and ubiquitination; (3) Intracellular signaling through recruitment of DVL and AXIN/GSK3B complex. Five PPPSP motifs provide signal amplification. Cell cycle-dependent regulation via CDK14/CCNY. Quantitative kinetic data available for key binding interactions (Kd values for DKK1, SOST, Wnt3a) and enzymatic parameters for GSK3B. Essential for modeling Wnt pathway dynamics, beta-catenin stabilization, and crosstalk with cell cycle machinery."
  }
